      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "This is a late bump (3 years!) but this is something I still need for some avatars. Many of my avatars use unlit black shaders where it is important for them to ignore lighting. The lack of an unlit shader makes this almost impossible, the current workaround (lightmapped shader) being far too expensive for what its worth.\nAppending the unlit shaders that come with unity as whitelisted quest shaders (solid color, texture, texture w/ multiplied color) would be very useful, and more performant for those niche cases that need them.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
